id: pm-zryb9d
title: "GH-971: health preflight collision diagnostics ignore declared command ownership"
description: "The runtime honors ScopedPreflightOverrideDefinition command ownership, but health collision analysis compares every registered preflight as global. Make diagnostics use the same effective ownership semantics so disjoint scoped preflights do not form an unresolvable warning clique."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[5]: "area:sdk",extensions,health,ownership,preflight
created_at: "2026-08-10T22:59:56.197Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-11T16:29:50.924Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-11T16:21:45.191Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-11T16:21:45.191Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: Two scoped preflight overrides collide only when their normalized command sets intersect; An unscoped override collides with every scoped or unscoped override because it is global; Health and runtime dispatch consume one shared ownership contract with fleet and negative-control coverage
parent: pm-ugqx
reporter: GitHub issue #971
severity: high
environment: pm 2026.8.10 with multiple installed extensions registering scoped preflight overrides
repro_steps: Install extensions with disjoint preflight command declarations and run pm health --full; observe a complete pairwise collision clique.
resolution: Aligned lazy activation and global collision inventory with ScopedPreflightOverrideDefinition command ownership.
expected_result: Health reports only preflight registrations that can contend for the same command.
actual_result: Disjoint scoped preflights activate only for their normalized commands and are excluded from global ownership; unscoped preflights remain global and conflict wherever applicable.
affected_version: 2026.8.10
component: Extension SDK health diagnostics
regression: true
customer_impact: Strict fleet health fails on valid extension composition and trains package authors to ignore ownership diagnostics.
