comments[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-10T22:59:56.197Z","harness:codex","Duplicate-check evidence 2026-08-11: all-status search found the closed GH-907 ownership implementation pm-miy5k6 and renderer collision lineage pm-6mjxgq, but no item owns the GH-971 health/runtime parity regression. Canonical source: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/971."
  "2026-08-11T15:05:33.659Z","harness:codex","TDD evidence 2026-08-11: two focused tests first failed because scoped preflight commands were absent from static activation and every preflight override counted as global. Static activation now consumes preflight_ownership and subtracts scoped registrations from global counts; 91 focused CLI/inventory/compose tests pass."
  "2026-08-11T15:37:20.948Z","harness:codex","Repository-wide verification evidence: exact coverage gate passed 486 files / 7,230 tests at 100% statements, branches, functions, and lines. Static quality, ESLint, jscpd zero clones, SDK snapshot, token-budget, context calibration, tracker measurement, graph composition, and record integrity gates passed."
  "2026-08-11T16:20:41.424Z","harness:codex","Final acceptance 2026-08-11: the linked 91-test activation, inventory, and SDK composition run passed in an isolated schema tracker. The repo-wide exact gate passed 7,234 tests at 100/100/100/100, and packed npx, package artifact, real Codex/Claude plugins, 10 external packages, contracts, docs, audit, and credential scan all passed."
  "2026-08-11T16:25:25.355Z","harness:codex","Release-candidate evidence: installed managed pm-changelog 2026.8.9 matches the latest npm version; replace-mode generation added this closed item to Unreleased with its canonical GitHub item link."
  "2026-08-11T16:29:50.924Z","harness:codex","Delivery lineage: included in broad PR #981 (https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/981), coordinated by pm-ajj4r7 through exact-head review, merge, and immutable release verification."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-11T16:20:40.952Z","harness:codex",Extension diagnostics are trustworthy only when static inventories and runtime dispatch share the same ownership semantics. A declared scoped contribution must be subtracted from the global bucket as well as added to its command bucket.
